{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HARNESS RUN 4 — 47 PASSED / 2 FAILED, up from 43/6. Run 30763838558, job id 91538992083, main @\n144bb02251, 1567.80s. Both remaining failures are understood and NEITHER is an unknown.\n\nFAILURE 1 — [04-transition-status]: the d067-5d2f-bcee-46ae defect, EXPECTED here because this run\npredates that fix. d067's two commits (8961f12664, 2ea5c3391d) have since MERGED, and harness run\n30765232591 is in flight against 2ea5c3391d to confirm the cell goes green.\n\nFAILURE 2 — THE INBOUND-ASSIGNEE CELL, AND IT IS THIS STORY'S TO FIX. Message:\n    FAILED (not a product finding): the store copy ALREADY maps jira/'admin' to\n    '26e2-d8e3-6077-4b94' before the pass runs, so a mapping afterwards would prove nothing about\n    this pass. The scrub is expected to leave no identity for the harness admin.\nREAD WHAT THAT MEANS BEFORE 'FIXING' IT: this is the REWRITTEN oracle working exactly as designed.\nThe old oracle compared ensure_identity_for's return against itself and could never fail. The\nrewrite added a SETUP assertion that the identity is ABSENT before the pass, precisely so a\npre-existing mapping cannot let the cell pass vacuously. On the real harness that precondition is\nviolated: the scrubbed store copy already carries an identity mapping for the harness admin user.\nSo the cell is REFUSING TO REPORT SUCCESS IT CANNOT JUSTIFY — the improvement this story wanted —\nrather than reporting a product defect. There is no DC bug here.\n\nTHE FIX IS IN THE ORACLE'S CHOICE OF SUBJECT, NOT IN RELAXING THE ASSERTION. Two candidate shapes,\nand whichever is taken must keep the setup assertion:\n  (a) drive the cell with a DC user that the scrub genuinely leaves unmapped, rather than the\n      harness ADMIN, whose identity the store copy legitimately carries from prior Cloud syncs; or\n  (b) have the cell scrub that one mapping as part of its own setup and assert the absence it just\n      established.\nDO NOT delete the setup assertion to make the cell green — that reinstates precisely the tautology\nthis story removed, and it would be the fourth unpassable-or-vacuous oracle this epic has found.\n\nREMAINING TO CLOSE THIS STORY: fix that oracle precondition, and confirm on one harness run that\nBOTH [04-transition-status] and the assignee cell are green. Everything else this story owed is\nmerged (1182, 1188, 1203, 1214, 1215, 1216)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785701855305818001,"uuid":"aa4e4f0c-4582-42c5-be4b-504fb09d488e"}